          "number": 2,
          "letter": "",
          "english": "Not so long ago, people would have turned up their noses at that kind of dedication to the job. As marketing professors Silvia Bellezza, Neeru Paharia, and Anat Keinan recently explained in Harvard Business Review (HBR), leisure time was once seen as an indicator of high social status, something attainable only for those at the top. Since the middle of the 20th century, though, things have turned the opposite way—these days, punishing hours at your desk, rather than days off, are seen as the mark of someone important.",
          "chinese": "就在不久以前，人们还会对那种对工作的投入嗤之以鼻。正如市场营销学教授 Silvia Bellezza、Neeru Paharia 和 Anat Keinan 近日在《哈佛商业评论》（HBR）中所解释的那样，休闲时间曾一度被视为社会地位高的标志，是只有位居顶层的人才能享有的东西。然而，自20世纪中叶以来，情况却朝相反的方向发展了——如今，人们把伏案工作的高强度长时间，而不是休假天数，视为某个重要人物的标志。",
